<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1H">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "08">
<configtype typenbr = "2">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1826002" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Spark Plug Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1826001">Spark Plug Removal and Installation:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
The iridium spark plug has a slender center electrode that is made of a material sensitive to mechanical forces. It may be damaged if handled carelessly.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not touch the center electrode of an iridium spark plug. Avoid cleaning it or adjusting its electrode gap.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<ptxt>
Check spark plug for:
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Electrode wear
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Carbon deposits
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Insulator damage
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Spark plug air gap
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<ptxt>
Check spark plug air gap “a” using special tool.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If out of specification of the air gap or any other abnormality is found with iridium spark plug, replace it with new plug.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1H204">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09930-77410">
09930–77410
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<spec-sdm>
<sdm-title>
Spark plug air gap
</sdm-title>
<sdm-part>
“a”
</sdm-part>
<sdm1>
<sdm-condition>
</sdm-condition>
<sdm-value>
0.7 to 0.8 mm (0.028 to 0.031 in.)
</sdm-value>
</sdm1>
</spec-sdm>
<spec-sdm>
<sdm-title>
Spark plug type
</sdm-title>
<sdm1>
<sdm-condition>
NGK
</sdm-condition>
<sdm-value>
ILZKR7N8S (Iridium)
</sdm-value>
</sdm1>
</spec-sdm>
